.TITLE "rm"

.DIV "DESCRIPTION"
Removes files or directories from the filesystem. It is a powerful tool that should be used with __caution__ as deletions are typically __permanent__.

.DIV "TLDR"
**rm file**
Removes a specific file from the current directory.
> __file__ the name of the file

**rm -r folder**
Removes a directory and all of its contents recursively.
> __-r__ recursive flag | __folder__ the target directory

**rm -f file**
Forcefully removes a file without prompting for confirmation.
> __-f__ force flag | __file__ the name of the file

**rm -i file**
Prompts for confirmation before removing each file.
> __-i__ interactive flag | __file__ the name of the file

**rm -v file**
Displays a message for every file that is removed.
> __-v__ verbose flag | __file__ the name of the file

.DIV "SUMMARY"
Always double-check your path before using __rm -r -f__, as it can delete large amounts of data without warning. Using the __-i__ flag is a good habit when working with critical production files.

.DIV "SEE ALSO"
**linux:mv**

